From 0509a2e1aa8beb17f9cd09be2a162fafc10a6a5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suharvest <suharvest@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 22:04:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] use v010 native qwen3 tts voice clone

Use the v0.10 Base voice-clone path (`cloneEncoderDir`) and forward
`ref_audio`/`ref_text` to the native runtime, which owns reference encoding and
ICL construction.

Keep the native export path portable as well: Code2Wav selects CUDA only when
available, and the Mimi clone encoder uses eager attention so current
Transformers can export its static speech-tokenizer bucket without a symbolic
SDPA guard failure.

Normalize streaming CLI PCM chunks according to the engine's actual waveform
dtype. Qwen3-TTS Code2Wav exports FP32, so interpreting its buffer as FP16
produces saturated noise even though the RVQ codes are correct.

The legacy `speaker_embedding_b64` request field remains accepted for protocol
compatibility, but is deliberately not decoded: v0.10 has no host-side
arbitrary speaker-embedding ABI. Requests containing it receive a warning and
the field is ignored; callers must migrate to `ref_audio` with optional
`ref_text`.

Signed-off-by: suharvest <suharvest@gmail.com>
